From bb54eea0d9780fa8f308f3b894911638c5314c77 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Vitaly Lipatov <lav@etersoft.ru>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 19:20:52 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 46/58] ACPI: IORT: recognize raw ACPI ancestors in named
 component lookup

IORT named-component lookup walks parents that may themselves be ACPI
namespace devices. ACPI_COMPANION() handles physical companions but does
not cover that raw ACPI-device case.

Use the previously added ACPI-device resolution helper while matching
the ancestor chain. This lets supplemental display/GPU children reach
the correct OEM named component without inventing a companion for their
raw ACPI parent. Stream selection and table validation remain in the
dedicated consumer-specific paths.
---
 drivers/acpi/arm64/iort.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/acpi/arm64/iort.c b/drivers/acpi/arm64/iort.c
index 3ee887b247bce3a72b7abdfb7a66383070403910..f5f3fe873afc2e97f2479bcad71d2d65cdca3d3b 100644
--- a/drivers/acpi/arm64/iort.c
+++ b/drivers/acpi/arm64/iort.c
@@ -282,7 +282,7 @@ static acpi_status iort_match_node_callback(struct acpi_iort_node *node,
 		 * start with.
 		 */
 		do {
-			adev = ACPI_COMPANION(cdev);
+			adev = acpi_companion_or_self(cdev);
 			if (adev)
 				break;
 
